module gunbc.v1_interpreter_primitive_surface

data v1_interpreter_primitive_surface_authority_note: String = "THE V1 INTERPRETER'S PRIMITIVE DISPATCH SURFACE, MADE ENUMERABLE. Before this carrier the surface had no roster anywhere: its only authority was string match arms inside the hand-maintained seed src/v1/stage0/src/v1_interpreter.rs, so 'which primitives does the interpreter provide' was a question no consumer could ask. That is why it was the fifth surface the primitive-identity census could not read, and why v1 deletion could not be sequenced honestly: you cannot show that nothing still needs a capability you cannot enumerate.\n\nTHE SURFACE IS SEVEN DISPATCH MECHANISMS ACROSS SIX FUNCTIONS. Measured against the tree rather than assumed: eval_builtin_inner; eval_algebra_method_inner; eval_call, which carries TWO separate mechanisms -- nine guard-predicated v4 std bridges (resolve_type_node, symbol_lexeme, concept_decl_facts_live and the rest, each fired only when its is_v4_*_bridge_call predicate holds) AND a native fold intercept -- both of which run BEFORE the free-call dispatch, which is why fold_list and the bridge names never reach the builtin registry; try_v2_std_collection_map_primitive_grounding; try_parse_table_memo_dispatch; and a lookup short-circuit inside eval_method_call. AN EARLIER REVISION OF THIS NOTE SAID SIX SITES AND MODELLED eval_call AS THE FOLD INTERCEPT ALONE, omitting all twelve bridge spellings; the omission was caught in review, and it is recorded here rather than quietly corrected because it is the precise failure this carrier exists to prevent -- a denominator asserted from the sites someone happened to read.\n\nTHE DENOMINATOR IS RECONCILED AGAINST THE WHOLE FILE, which is what makes it checkable rather than a list of what was noticed. v1_interpreter.rs carries 209 quoted match-arm lines in total. 170 of them are primitive dispatch and are rows here: 113 in the eval_builtin_inner macro authority, 39 algebra methods, 14 in eval_call (12 bridges + 2 fold), 2 map-grounding, 2 parse-table. One further arm, the eval_method_call lookup short-circuit, is an if rather than a match arm and so appears in no line count. The remaining 39 lines are deliberately NOT primitive dispatch and are named so the residue is not mistaken for an omission: 12 in match_pattern (pattern kinds), 5 each in map_shell_outputs, map_file_outputs and dispatch_rest, 3 each in resolve_auth and expectation_from_declared_arg, 2 each in dispatch_file and rest_tls_posture_interp_disposition, and 2 nested inside eval_builtin_inner arm bodies rather than being arms themselves. Those dispatch on HTTP methods, TLS postures, auth kinds and output channels -- transport and value vocabulary, not primitive names.\n\nSERVICE OPERATIONS ARE NOT ARMS, and that is a finding rather than an omission. eval_service_call resolves Service.Op against ctx.service_ops, which is built from the DECLARED .dag corpus, so that population is already enumerable as data and is deliberately outside this roster's denominator. The interpreter contributes exactly one service-name dispatch of its own -- the Filesystem.Read hermetic checkout carve-out -- plus transport realizations, which dispatch on transport and HTTP method values rather than on primitive names. Only the carve-out is a row here.\n\nHOW EACH FORM IS KNOWN, WHICH IS THE FRONTIER. FreeCall rows from eval_builtin_inner are DERIVED: that arm list is now a single macro authority in v1_interpreter.rs from which both the dispatch and this roster expand, so an arm without a roster row and a roster row without an arm are both unwritable rather than reconciled afterwards (DESIGN 5, construction over validation). No live-tree scan of Rust source is involved and none is wanted: a regex interpreting hand-written match arms would leave the denominator in Rust while adding a second thing that can be wrong.\n\nTHE REMAINING ROWS ARE DECLARED BY HAND and can therefore go stale. That is counted (v1_interpreter_declared_arm_count) rather than hidden, and the dissolution trigger is specific, not aspirational: apply the v1_builtin_arms macro shape to eval_algebra_method_inner (uniform literal arms today, so it is the same mechanical transformation), then to the three small dispatches, then delete each declared block as its projection lands. The Filesystem.Read carve-out is the one row that stays declared until the hermetic carve-out itself dissolves. Absence from a declared block is NOT evidence that an arm does not exist.\n\nROWS CARRY THE ARM'S OWN FACTS ONLY. There is deliberately no primitive-identity field, not even an optional one: an arm that joins to no known primitive must remain representable, because that population is exactly what a primitive-identity join needs to discover. A roster whose shape forbade recording an unjoined arm would be complete by construction and useless as a denominator. This carrier answers WHICH ARMS EXIST; which primitive each one realizes belongs to the join.\n\nONE ROW PER (FORM, SPELLING); ALIASES SHARE AN ARM IDENTITY. length, count and size are one arm under three rows, so they cannot disagree by construction. A spelling appearing under two different arm identities in the SAME form is unreachable code, because the earlier arm always wins. A spelling appearing under two different FORMS is two genuine implementations: lookup is the live specimen, dispatched both by the eval_method_call short-circuit and by an algebra arm the short-circuit shadows."

data v1_interpreter_source_path: String = "src/v1/stage0/src/v1_interpreter.rs"

type InterpreterDispatchForm
  = FreeCall
  | MethodCall
  | ServiceDispatch
  | NativeSpecial
  | UnknownForm { label: NonEmptyStr }

type InterpreterPrimitiveArmId {
  identity: NonEmptyStr
}

type ArmEnumeration
  = DerivedFromDispatch
  | DeclaredHere { dissolve_on: NonEmptyStr }

type InterpreterPrimitiveDispatchArm {
  arm: InterpreterPrimitiveArmId
  form: InterpreterDispatchForm
  authored_spelling: NonEmptyStr
  realization_module: NonEmptyStr
  dispatch_symbol: NonEmptyStr
  enumeration: ArmEnumeration
}

type ShapeDerivability
  = ShapeNotDerivableFromDispatch
  | ShapeDerivedFromDispatch

fn v1_interpreter_arm_shape_derivability() -> ShapeDerivability {
  ShapeNotDerivableFromDispatch
}

fn decode_dispatch_form(label: String) -> InterpreterDispatchForm {
  match label {
    "FreeCall" => FreeCall
    "MethodCall" => MethodCall
    "NativeSpecial" => NativeSpecial
    "ServiceDispatch" => ServiceDispatch
    _ => UnknownForm { label: label }
  }
}

fn form_is_unknown(form: InterpreterDispatchForm) -> Bool {
  match form {
    UnknownForm { label } => true
    FreeCall => false
    MethodCall => false
    NativeSpecial => false
    ServiceDispatch => false
  }
}

fn v1_interpreter_derived_arms() -> List<InterpreterPrimitiveDispatchArm> {
  interpreter_dispatch_arm_rows()
    |> map(r => InterpreterPrimitiveDispatchArm {
      arm: InterpreterPrimitiveArmId { identity: r.arm_identity },
      form: decode_dispatch_form(label: r.dispatch_form),
      authored_spelling: r.authored_spelling,
      realization_module: "v1_interpreter",
      dispatch_symbol: r.dispatch_symbol,
      enumeration: DerivedFromDispatch,
    })
}

fn v1_interpreter_free_call_arms() -> List<InterpreterPrimitiveDispatchArm> {
  v1_interpreter_derived_arms() |> filter(r => r.form == FreeCall)
}

fn v1_interpreter_method_call_arms() -> List<InterpreterPrimitiveDispatchArm> {
  v1_interpreter_derived_arms() |> filter(r => r.form == MethodCall)
}

fn v1_interpreter_unknown_form_arms() -> List<InterpreterPrimitiveDispatchArm> {
  v1_interpreter_derived_arms() |> filter(r => form_is_unknown(form: r.form))
}

fn v1_interpreter_declared_arms() -> List<InterpreterPrimitiveDispatchArm> {
  [
    InterpreterPrimitiveDispatchArm {
      arm: InterpreterPrimitiveArmId { identity: "method_call_short_circuit.lookup" },
      form: MethodCall,
      authored_spelling: "lookup",
      realization_module: "v1_interpreter",
      dispatch_symbol: "eval_method_call",
      enumeration: DeclaredHere {
        dissolve_on: "eval_method_call's lookup short-circuit is an if-guard rather than a match arm, so it has no token authority to expand from. It dissolves when the short-circuit is either deleted in favour of the algebra arm it shadows, or rewritten as an arm of a v1_method_short_circuit_arms macro in the shape the other five sites now use.",
      },
    },
    InterpreterPrimitiveDispatchArm {
      arm: InterpreterPrimitiveArmId { identity: "service_dispatch.Filesystem.Read" },
      form: ServiceDispatch,
      authored_spelling: "Filesystem.Read",
      realization_module: "v1_interpreter",
      dispatch_symbol: "eval_service_call",
      enumeration: DeclaredHere {
        dissolve_on: "the hermetic checkout carve-out in eval_service_call is the interpreter's only service-name dispatch of its own; every other service operation resolves against ctx.service_ops from the declared .dag corpus. This row dissolves when the carve-out does.",
      },
    },
  ]
}

fn v1_interpreter_primitive_arms() -> List<InterpreterPrimitiveDispatchArm> {
  v1_interpreter_derived_arms() |> concat(v1_interpreter_declared_arms())
}

fn distinct_strings(xs: List<String>) -> List<String> {
  xs |> fold(init: [], f: (acc, x) => if acc |> any(y => y == x) { acc } else { acc |> concat([x]) })
}

fn v1_interpreter_derived_arm_count() -> Int {
  count(v1_interpreter_derived_arms())
}

fn v1_interpreter_declared_arm_count() -> Int {
  count(v1_interpreter_declared_arms())
}

fn v1_interpreter_row_count() -> Int {
  count(v1_interpreter_primitive_arms())
}

fn dispatch_site_count() -> Int {
  count(distinct_strings(xs: v1_interpreter_primitive_arms() |> map(r => r.dispatch_symbol)))
}

fn distinct_arm_identity_count() -> Int {
  count(distinct_strings(xs: v1_interpreter_primitive_arms() |> map(r => r.arm.identity)))
}

fn authored_spelling_count() -> Int {
  count(distinct_strings(xs: v1_interpreter_primitive_arms() |> map(r => r.authored_spelling)))
}

fn spelling_arm_identities(rows: List<InterpreterPrimitiveDispatchArm>, spelling: String) -> List<String> {
  rows |> filter(r => r.authored_spelling == spelling) |> map(r => r.arm.identity)
}

fn form_has_no_shadowed_spelling(rows: List<InterpreterPrimitiveDispatchArm>) -> Bool {
  rows |> all(r =>
    count(
      spelling_arm_identities(rows: rows, spelling: r.authored_spelling)
        |> filter(id => id != r.arm.identity)) == 0)
}

fn shadowed_spellings(rows: List<InterpreterPrimitiveDispatchArm>) -> List<String> {
  let shadowed = rows
    |> filter(r =>
      count(
        spelling_arm_identities(rows: rows, spelling: r.authored_spelling)
          |> filter(id => id != r.arm.identity)) > 0)
    |> map(r => r.authored_spelling)
  distinct_strings(xs: shadowed)
}

fn row_key(row: InterpreterPrimitiveDispatchArm) -> String {
  row.dispatch_symbol
    |> concat(":")
    |> concat(row.arm.identity)
    |> concat(":")
    |> concat(row.authored_spelling)
}

fn duplicate_row_keys(rows: List<InterpreterPrimitiveDispatchArm>) -> List<String> {
  let dupes = rows
    |> filter(r =>
      count(rows |> filter(o =>
        o.authored_spelling == r.authored_spelling
          && o.arm.identity == r.arm.identity
          && o.dispatch_symbol == r.dispatch_symbol)) > 1)
    |> map(r => row_key(row: r))
  distinct_strings(xs: dupes)
}

fn v1_interpreter_cross_form_spellings() -> List<String> {
  let rows = v1_interpreter_primitive_arms()
  let cross = rows
    |> filter(r =>
      count(rows |> filter(o => o.authored_spelling == r.authored_spelling && o.form != r.form)) > 0)
    |> map(r => r.authored_spelling)
  distinct_strings(xs: cross)
}

data arm_accepted_shape_gap_note: String = "ARITY IS NOT DERIVABLE FROM THIS DISPATCH, and ArmAcceptedShape is a coproduct rather than an Int so that the gap is representable instead of guessed. Arm bodies reach for positional.first(), positional.as_slice() patterns, and byte-vector coercions, so nothing structural in the arm states how many arguments it accepts. Any number written here would be a hand transcription that rots silently the first time a body changes, which is the decorative-roster failure this carrier exists to avoid. A typed absence is countable; a fabricated arity is not. DISSOLVE-ON: the R1 step where the v1_builtin_arms arm list carries an explicit parameter spec beside each body, at which point arity expands from the same tokens as the spelling and this type gains real inhabitants."

data derived_versus_declared_note: String = "WHICH ROWS ARE REAL BY CONSTRUCTION. v1_interpreter_free_call_arms is DERIVED: it projects interpreter_free_call_arm_rows, which expands from the same macro tokens as the dispatch itself, so adding an arm without a row and adding a row without an arm are both unwritable. v1_interpreter_method_call_arms, v1_interpreter_native_special_arms and v1_interpreter_service_dispatch_arms are DECLARED by hand and can go stale; they are counted separately by v1_interpreter_declared_arm_count so the frontier is a number rather than an impression. The owning roadmap row is v1-interpreter-primitive-roster, and v1-interpreter-quarantine depends on it. DISSOLVE-ON, per block: apply the v1_builtin_arms macro shape to eval_algebra_method_inner first (its arms are uniform string literals today, so it is the same mechanical transformation that already succeeded on eval_builtin_inner), then to eval_call, try_v2_std_collection_map_primitive_grounding and try_parse_table_memo_dispatch; delete each declared block as its projection lands. The Filesystem.Read row stays declared until the hermetic checkout carve-out itself dissolves."

data shadowed_spelling_semantics_note: String = "WHAT form_has_no_shadowed_spelling ACTUALLY DECIDES. A spelling reached by more than one ARM IDENTITY within a single form is unreachable code, because the earlier arm always wins the match. Alias spellings are deliberately NOT this: they share one arm identity, which is precisely why length, count and size cannot disagree with each other. A spelling appearing under two different FORMS is a third thing again and is not a defect at all -- it is two genuine implementations of one name, which v1_interpreter_cross_form_spellings derives and a primitive-identity join must reconcile rather than assume away. lookup is the live specimen."

data added_hand_rust_accounting_note: String = "WHAT THIS ADDED TO THE SEED, STATED PLAINLY RATHER THAN IMPLIED AWAY. The macro conversion of eval_builtin_inner moves 1,149 lines of existing arm bodies verbatim and adds no logic; the genuinely NEW hand-Rust is one dispatch arm, interpreter_free_call_arm_rows, plus the three macro_rules wrappers. So this change does NOT shrink the hand-Rust census and must not be counted as if it did. What it buys is the precondition for shrinking it: v1_interpreter.rs is hand-maintained and absent from gunbc.stage0_emit_model generated_stage0_files, and it cannot be retired until what it provides can be enumerated, which is why v1-interpreter-quarantine now depends on v1-interpreter-primitive-roster. THE ADDED RUST DISSOLVES ON TWO TRIGGERS, both named rather than deferred to someday: the macro wrappers and the reading arm are deleted wholesale when v1-interpreter-delete lands, since the file goes with them; and before that, the R1 step -- generating the dispatch FROM this roster rather than deriving the roster from the dispatch -- moves the denominator out of Rust entirely, at which point the declared blocks in this carrier delete too. Neither trigger is speculative: both are existing roadmap rows with edges already in the authority."
